.\" send-matrix-mail manual page
.\"
.TH SEND-MATRIX-MAIL 1 "July 2026" "send-matrix-mail 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
send-matrix-mail \- sendmail-compatible Matrix message delivery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B send-matrix-mail
[\fI\-t\fR] [\fI\-f\fR \fIaddr\fR] [\fI\-C\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fIrecipient\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B send-matrix-mail
reads an RFC 5322 email message from stdin, resolves recipients to Matrix
delivery targets, and posts an m.text message to each unique room. It is
designed as a drop-in replacement for /usr/sbin/sendmail for use by cron,
PHP, monitoring systems, and scripts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t
Extract recipients from the To:, Cc:, and Bcc: headers of the message.
.TP
.BI \-f " addr"
Set the envelope from (author) address.
.TP
.BI \-F " name"
Set the sender full name (accepted but ignored for compatibility).
.TP
.B \-i, \-oi
Ignore dots in stdin (always on — reads to EOF).
.TP
.BI \-C " path"
Path to the TOML configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of flags.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
0
Message delivered or safely queued.
.TP
65
Input format error.
.TP
67
No deliverable targets.
.TP
73
Spool write failure (disk full, permissions).
.TP
78
Configuration error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/send-matrix-mail/sendmailrc.toml
System-wide configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/send-matrix-mail/sendmailrc.toml
User configuration.
.SH AUTHOR
Crooy.com B.V.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR msmtp (1),
.IR sendmail (8)